# Compliance Analyst - KYB
United Kingdom, London / Full-time: Remote / Compliance
Apply for this Job
Binance is a leading global blockchain ecosystem behind the world’s largest cryptocurrency exchange by trading volume and registered users. We are trusted by 300+ million people in 100+ countries for our industry-leading security, user fund transparency, trading engine speed, deep liquidity, and an unmatched portfolio of digital-asset products. Binance offerings range from trading and finance to education, research, payments, institutional services, Web3 features, and more. We leverage the power of digital assets and blockchain to build an inclusive financial ecosystem to advance the freedom of money and improve financial access for people around the world.
### Responsabilities:
- Act as a point of escalation and subject matter expert for Corporate onboarding cases;
- Ability to take on and lead special assignments and projects;
- Take the lead on adhoc QA checks to support the regional team;
- Identify and propose procedure and process enhancements;
- Work with the team lead and Manager for ongoing assessments, assisting with compliance reviews, and ongoing or ad hoc reviews;
- Work closely with MLRO’s, Account Managers/ VIP and other key stakeholders within the business;
- Proficiency in compliance applications and programmes such as Worldcheck etc;
- Good knowledge on provisions of local laws, directives, regulations and otherwise standards applicable to subject persons and knowledge of upcoming regulation of virtual currency policies is a strong plus;
- Good proficiency in conducting customer risk assessments, periodic/trigger reviews and enhanced due diligence;
- Identification and documentation of unusual activity or AML flags;
- Participate in internal and external training programs related to AML/CFT and other subjects that may form part of the day to day work requirements.
### Requirements:
- At least 3+ years’ directly related experience in a compliance role with a substantial knowledge of relevant rules and regulations and the day-to-day compliance affairs;
- Strong experience in corporate onboarding and different corporate structure types;
- Demonstrated ability to write effectively;
- Superior organizational skills;
- Strong communication skills;
- ACAMS desirable.
**Why Binance**
• Shape the future with the world’s leading blockchain ecosystem
• Collaborate with world-class talent in a user-centric global organization with a flat structure
• Tackle unique, fast-paced projects with autonomy in an innovative environment
• Thrive in a results-driven workplace with opportunities for career growth and continuous learning
• Competitive salary and company benefits
• Work-from-home arrangement (the arrangement may vary depending on the work nature of the business team)
Binance is committed to being an equal opportunity employer. We believe that having a diverse workforce is fundamental to our success.
*By submitting a job application, you confirm that you have read and agree to our* ***Candidate Privacy Notice****.*

# Bid Leader
**About Us**
At Braden, we are driven by the extraordinary potential of our colleagues to tackle even the most complex challenges. We turn obstacles into opportunities, and our shared commitment to a sustainable future starts with each of us. Every day, our team collaborates to share knowledge and improve wherever possible, creating lasting benefits for generations to come.
With design offices in Europe, the United Kingdom, and North America, Braden combines 100 years of innovation with a strong dedication to customer excellence. We deliver performance and product efficiency for customers in power generation, oil & gas, petrochemical, and industrial sectors. Our offices are strategically positioned to provide global access to our expertise while maintaining a local focus in everything we do. We are a leading supplier of auxiliary equipment for major gas turbine OEMs and a trusted provider of aftermarket products and services for gas turbine operators worldwide.
**Role, Team & Location**
We are looking for an experienced and commercially minded **Bid Leader** to join our Product Solutions team in Cramlington office in the UK. In this role, you take ownership of assigned opportunities from qualification through proposal submission and negotiation. You bring together technical, commercial, and customer requirements to develop competitive solutions that create value for both Braden and our customers.
Reporting to the Business Unit Director Product Solutions, you work closely with the Sales Director, Engineering, Costing, Project Management, Purchasing, Manufacturing, Quality, and other key stakeholders. You will also provide day-to-day direction to the Engineers supporting your bids. This is a key role for someone who combines a strong technical foundation with commercial judgement and enjoys working at the centre of complex customer opportunities.
**Key Responsibilities**
As a Bid Leader, you take the lead in turning customer opportunities into strong and competitive technical-commercial proposals. You assess customer requirements, define the bid strategy, identify key risks and opportunities, and coordinate the people and expertise needed to deliver a high-quality proposal. You work closely with engineering and commercial teams to develop technical solutions that meet customer expectations while remaining commercially sound and aligned with Braden’s objectives. Throughout the bid process, you maintain oversight of scope, pricing assumptions, contractual requirements, risks, and proposal quality.
As the primary customer contact during the bid phase, you lead technical and commercial discussions, manage clarifications, and support negotiations to achieve balanced and mutually beneficial outcomes. Internally, you bring teams together, provide direction, and ensure that decisions and priorities are clear. Beyond individual bids, you contribute to improving the way we work by sharing knowledge, developing best practices, and supporting the growth of Application Engineers and future technical-commercial talent.
**What You Bring**
**Experience & Education**
* HNC/HND/FdEng in Mechanical Engineering or an equivalent technical discipline; a Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field is desirable;
* Experience in bid management, applications engineering, proposal engineering, technical sales, or a comparable technical-commercial role;
* Experience leading or coordinating complex technical-commercial proposals;
* Strong experience working directly with customers, suppliers, and cross-functional teams;
* Experience reviewing customer specifications, commercial requirements, and contractual terms and conditions.
**Skills & Competencies**
* Strong technical understanding and the ability to review, develop, and challenge engineering solutions;
* Commercial judgement with the ability to identify risk and develop balanced solutions;
* Strong customer relationship management and stakeholder coordination skills;
* Effective technical-commercial communication and negotiation skills;
* Strong analytical, organisational, and problem-solving capabilities;
* Ability to interpret technical documentation, engineering drawings, and customer specifications;
* Good understanding of engineering principles, manufacturing practices, and fabrication methods;
* Knowledge of filtration, acoustics, airflow, and related equipment applications is highly valuable;
* Excellent command of English, both written and spoken;
* Independent, collaborative, and comfortable taking ownership;
* A growth mindset and willingness to challenge constructively while remaining open to feedback.
**What You Will Get**
At Braden, you will take on a key role in delivering complex, international projects within a technically driven environment. You will have ownership, responsibility, and the opportunity to make a direct impact on project success and customer satisfaction.
* A full-time position within an international and growing organisation;
* A competitive salary, aligned with your experience and level;
* A culture of openness and short communication lines;
* Strong team culture;
* Opportunities to career growth within our international organisation;
* A dynamic and technically challenging work environment with diverse, international projects;
* A high level of responsibility and autonomy in managing projects end-to-end;
* Close collaboration with multidisciplinary teams across engineering, operations, and commercial functions;
* A professional and structured organisation where continuous improvement and quality are key.
If you are looking for a role where you can take ownership, drive results, and operate at the centre of technical project execution, this is your opportunity.
**Why Join Us?**
At Braden, you will be part of a dedicated team that shares a common vision for sustainable and innovative solutions. We offer an inclusive, collaborative work environment where your contributions are valued and recognized. Here, you will have the opportunity to work with talented professionals who share your commitment. Ready to join a forward-thinking team that values innovation and sustainability?
Apply today to become part of Braden and make a meaningful impact on our financial stability and long-term success!

# Technical Proposal Engineer
**About Us**
At Braden, we are driven by the extraordinary potential of our colleagues to tackle even the most complex challenges. We turn obstacles into opportunities, and our shared commitment to a sustainable future starts with each of us. Every day, our team collaborates to share knowledge and improve wherever possible, creating lasting benefits for generations to come.
With design offices in Europe, the United Kingdom, and North America, Braden combines 100 years of innovation with a strong dedication to customer excellence. We deliver performance and product efficiency for customers in power generation, oil & gas, petrochemical, and industrial sectors. Our offices are strategically positioned to provide global access to our expertise while maintaining a local focus in everything we do. We are a leading supplier of auxiliary equipment for major gas turbine OEMs and a trusted provider of aftermarket products and services for gas turbine operators worldwide.
**Role, Team & Location**
We are looking for a technically driven and commercially aware **Technical Proposal Engineer** to join our Product Solutions team in Cramlington UK. In this role, you will support our Bid Leaders in developing competitive technical and commercial proposals for our customers. You will translate customer specifications into practical engineering solutions, perform technical evaluations and calculations, and help ensure that every proposed solution is compliant, cost-effective, and fit for purpose.
You will work closely with Bid Leaders, Costing, Engineering, Purchasing, Project Management, and key suppliers across multiple customer accounts. This position offers a unique opportunity to combine your engineering knowledge with the commercial side of our business and develop your career towards either a technical specialist or future bid leadership role.
**Key Responsibilities**
As a Technical Proposal Engineer, you play an important role in turning customer requirements into technically sound and competitive solutions. You review specifications, engineering drawings, and technical documentation, perform calculations and evaluations, and work with Bid Leaders and Engineering to determine the most suitable solution during the proposal stage. You bring together technical input from different disciplines, suppliers, and internal stakeholders and support the preparation of technical proposals, compliance documentation, clarifications, and cost estimates. You will also engage with customers and suppliers on technical matters, helping to identify deviations, resolve questions, and ensure that proposed equipment meets the intended application and operating requirements.
Once an order is awarded, you help ensure a smooth handover to the project team by transferring the relevant technical requirements, calculations, and bid clarifications. Throughout your work, you look for opportunities to improve quality, efficiency, and the way we develop technical solutions.
**What You Bring**
**Experience & Education**
* HNC/HND/FdEng in Mechanical Engineering or an equivalent technical discipline; a Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering is desirable;
* Experience in engineering, applications engineering, manufacturing, proposal support, or a related technical role;
* Experience working within a technical, manufacturing, or project-driven environment would be advantageous.
**Skills & Competencies**
* Good understanding of engineering principles, manufacturing practices, and fabrication methods;
* Ability to interpret customer specifications, engineering drawings, and technical documentation;
* Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to translate requirements into practical technical solutions;
* Commercial awareness and an interest in developing technical-commercial proposals;
* Strong organisational and communication skills and the ability to coordinate across multiple disciplines and stakeholders;
* Proficiency in Microsoft Office; basic knowledge of Autodesk tools is desirable;
* Excellent command of English, both written and spoken;
* Comfortable working independently while collaborating closely with colleagues, customers, and suppliers;
* A proactive mindset and willingness to further develop both your technical and commercial capabilities.
**What You Will Get**
At Braden, you will take on a key role in delivering complex, international projects within a technically driven environment. You will have ownership, responsibility, and the opportunity to make a direct impact on project success and customer satisfaction.
* A full-time position within an international and growing organisation;
* A competitive salary, aligned with your experience and level;
* A culture of openness and short communication lines;
* Strong team culture;
* Opportunities to career growth within our international organisation;
* A dynamic and technically challenging work environment with diverse, international projects;
* A high level of responsibility and autonomy in managing projects end-to-end;
* Close collaboration with multidisciplinary teams across engineering, operations, and commercial functions;
* A professional and structured organisation where continuous improvement and quality are key.
If you are looking for a role where you can take ownership, drive results, and operate at the centre of technical project execution, this is your opportunity.
**Why Join Us?**
At Braden, you will be part of a dedicated team that shares a common vision for sustainable and innovative solutions. We offer an inclusive, collaborative work environment where your contributions are valued and recognized. Here, you will have the opportunity to work with talented professionals who share your commitment. Ready to join a forward-thinking team that values innovation and sustainability?
Apply today to become part of Braden and make a meaningful impact on our financial stability and long-term success!

Business analyst (fintech) [2508]
3-5 years of experience • Full-time, Remote work • English - Advanced (C1) • Ukrainian - Native
We are looking for an experienced and proactive **Business analyst** to join our team at Dataforest and lead a long-term, high-scale FinTech project.
About the Project:
Our client is building a powerful B2B SaaS platform designed to revolutionize chargeback management, featuring enterprise-grade API integrations (Ethoca, Verifi), seamless payment processor connections (Stripe, Shopify, Braintree), and real-time dispute alerts. We are actively developing and scaling multiple product streams, including Business Health, Dispute Management, and others.
**You’ll be a great fit if you have:**
- 5+ years of experience in system, functional, or business analysis;
- English: Advanced and higher;
- Deep expertise in key business analysis techniques, requirement management tools, and standardizing BA documentation;
- Solid understanding of SDLC and Agile development processes;
- Strong hands-on experience in business process modeling (BPMN, UML) and domain-driven design;
- Proven proficiency in driving Discovery phases, extracting high-level business vision, and translating it into actionable roadmaps and specs;
- Advanced skills in drafting business (BRD), functional (SRS), and technical requirement specifications;
- Extensive experience in working with key business stakeholders and C-level executives, leading requirement elicitation and facilitation sessions;
- Exceptional critical thinking, problem-solving, and conflict-resolution skills;
- Ability to independently decompose complex system workflows and domain logic into manageable tasks;
- Strong technical background with a clear understanding of web development concepts, enterprise system integrations, and API design;
**- Practical experience using modern AI tools (ChatGPT, Claude, Copilot, etc.) to accelerate requirement generation, documentation, and analysis workflows.**
**Would be a plus:**
- Prior experience in FinTech, PayTech, Chargeback, or Payments domain;
- Experience working with projects that integrate AI/ML features or LLM API solutions;
- Hands-on experience with SQL and data modeling;
- Experience with integration-heavy B2B SaaS projects and payment gateway APIs (e.g., Stripe, Braintree).
**What you’ll do:**
- Serving as the primary point of contact for stakeholders to elicit, clarify, and validate complex product requirements;
- Leading the end-to-end requirement lifecycle: from high-level discovery down to backlog grooming, user story mapping, and detailing acceptance criteria;
- Visualizing complex FinTech workflows, business processes, and data models for multi-stream engineering teams;
- Advising stakeholders on industry best practices, platform capabilities, and optimal product solutions;
- Performing market research and domain analysis to contribute to product strategy and features elaboration;
- Communicating project vision and closely aligning requirements with System Architects, Tech Leads, and engineering teams;
- Actively participating in presale estimations, discovery activities, and scope definition for new product streams;
**- Drive & improve AI-driven BA practices: Leverage AI tools to speed up requirement drafting, analyze complex domain data, optimize BA artifacts, and enhance delivery processes.**
**We ensure your growth with:**
- Opportunity to work with the high-skilled engineering team on challenging projects;
- Interesting projects with new technologies;
- Great networking opportunities with international clients, challenging tasks;
- Building interesting projects from scratch using new technologies;
- Personal and professional development opportunities;
- Competitive salary fixed in USD;
- Paid vacation and sick leaves;
- Flexible work schedule;
- Friendly working environment with minimal hierarchy;
- Team building activities, corporate events.

