## Administrative Assistant
Apply
: United Kingdom, Kendal Fell
: Full time
: Posted Today
: End Date: September 11, 2026 (6 days left to apply)
: WD229029
Flex is the diversified manufacturing partner of choice that helps market-leading brands design, build and deliver innovative products that improve the world.
A career at Flex offers the opportunity to make a difference and invest in your growth in a respectful, inclusive, and collaborative environment. If you are excited about a role but don't meet every bullet point, we encourage you to apply and join us to create the extraordinary.
## Job Summary
* Organising travel for clients, directors and employees including flights, rail and hotel bookings worldwide;
* Being the first point of contact for visitors and clients including client hospitality; meeting and greeting, providing refreshments and catering;
* Managing budgets and ordering office materials;
* Answering the all incoming calls and directing them appropriately;
* Franking and posting all mail involving runs to the Post Office/Bank;
* Organising Courier shipments and tracking deliveries;
* Assisting Production and HR with daily administration tasks;
* Managing the Meeting Rooms Calendar;
* General up keep of meeting rooms, offices and kitchens;
* Assist the Service Centre with travel booking and coordinating of engineers;
* Updating service centre training records;
* Compiling data and assisting with site entry requirements;
* Any general administration duties as requested by the Heads or Department or the Office Manager.

**Job title:** Regional Manager - Ireland
**Location:** Field based – Northern Ireland
We are looking for a Regional Manager to cover both the Republic of Ireland and Northern Ireland, based in one of those locations. **Please apply for this position only if you are available/interested in being based in the Northern Ireland location.**
**Why Join HSB?**
We don’t just inspect—we protect. At HSB, you’ll join a team with a clear purpose, strong values, and a supportive culture where your expertise is respected and your contributions matter. From flexible working to wellbeing support, we invest in you so you can bring your best self to work—every day.
Apply today and become part of a company that doesn’t just engineer safety—but inspires trust.
**What You’ll Be Doing**
As a Regional Manager, you will lead a team of Engineering Surveyors across the Republic of Ireland and Northern Ireland, ensuring the delivery of exceptional customer service, operational excellence, and regulatory compliance. You'll work closely with Operations Managers and Technical Teams to ensure contractual commitments are achieved while creating an engaged, motivated, and high-performing workforce. You will be responsible for resource planning, performance management, recruitment activities, customer satisfaction, financial performance, and maintaining the highest standards of safety and service delivery within your region.
**What Makes This Role Special**
* Leadership impact: Lead and inspire a team of engineering professionals who make a difference every day;
* Business ownership: Take full responsibility for the operational and financial performance of your region, including P&L accountability;
* Growth opportunity: Play a key role in supporting business growth ambitions across Ireland while developing your own career;
* Field-based leadership: Work closely with your team in the field, providing coaching, support, and visible leadership;
* Trusted brand: Join a business recognised for technical excellence, customer service, and innovation as part of the wider Munich Re Group.
**What You Bring**
* Proven leadership experience managing field-based engineering or service delivery teams;
* Strong people management skills with the ability to motivate, coach, and develop high-performing teams;
* Excellent stakeholder and customer relationship management capabilities;
* Strong commercial awareness with experience managing budgets, performance metrics, and business objectives;
* Excellent planning and organisational skills, with the ability to effectively balance resources and workloads;
* A confident and proactive approach with a strong focus on results and continuous improvement;
* Commitment to maintaining and promoting a positive safety culture.
**What You’ll Need**
* Demonstrable experience leading field-based engineering or service-oriented teams;
* Engineering qualification;
* GCSE Maths and English (or equivalent);
* Strong understanding of KPI management and operational performance delivery;
* Knowledge of regulations including LOLER, PSSR, PUWER, COSHH, and Safety, Health and Welfare at Work Regulations would be advantageous;
* Previous experience within engineering inspection, lifting equipment, pressure systems, LEV systems, power presses, or related engineering disciplines would be advantageous;
* Holder of a full UK or Irish driving licence with no more than 6 penalty points.
**What We Offer**
In addition to a competitive salary and excellent work-life balance, you'll benefit from an industry-leading rewards package:
* 25 days Annual Leave + Bank Holidays + 2 Well-being days each year
* Ability to buy or sell leave.
* Up to 13% Pension contribution (9% non-contributory plus up to 4% matching contribution).
* Eligibility for an Annual Bonus up to 15% (dependent on Group performance)
* Private Medical & Dental (options to add family members at discounted rates)
* Life Assurance of six times salary
* Wellbeing and Development Scheme + EAP + Health Assessments (subject to scheme eligibility)
* Study & continuing Professional Development Support
* Choice of company vehicle or car allowance
* Access to Salary Sacrifice Car scheme
* Access to a range of discounted benefits such as critical illness cover and mortgage advisory services.
**Diversity, Equity & Inclusion**
At HSB, Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion foster innovation and resilience and enable us to act braver and better. Embracing the power of DEI is at the core of who we are. We recognise diversity can be multi-dimensional, intersectional, and complex, so we want to build a diverse workforce that includes a wide range of racial, ethnic, sexual, and gender identities; economic and geographic backgrounds; physical abilities; ages; life, school, and career experiences; and political, religious, and personal beliefs. Additionally, we are committed to building an equitable and inclusive work environment where this diversity is celebrated, valued, and has equitable opportunities to succeed.
All candidates in consideration for any role can request a reasonable adjustment at any point in our recruitment process. You can request an adjustment by speaking to your Talent Acquisition contact.

Ocean Infinity is seeking a OT/Marine Cyber Security Engineer.
As our OT/Marine Cyber Security Engineer you will own cyber and information security for operational technology. You will work inside the Cyber team and alongside the engineering and asset groups who design and build these systems, getting security into new technology as it is mobilised and tested, owning the regulatory and class controls that apply, and leading OT and vessel incident response. This is a cyber and information security role; physical security is a coordinated interface rather than the main focus.
**What you will do**
* Own the OT and marine cyber security programme for the operational technology Ocean Infinity designs, builds and maintains, including IEC 62443 zone and conduit design across in-scope vessels, robotic and autonomous systems.
* Engage early as new technology is mobilised and fielded, so that cyber and information security is designed in from first deployment rather than added later.
* Test new and evolving technology, validate its security through development and deployment, and feed findings back to the engineering teams.
* Contribute to blast radius and containment design, so that the impact of any single compromise across autonomous, robotic and vessel systems is limited by design.
* Lead OT and vessel incident response, from identification through containment and recovery to post-incident review, in coordination with the wider Cyber team and vessel stakeholders.
* Own the regulatory and class controls that apply to the OT estate, including DNV class notation and autonomous system assurance (AROS certification), acting as the primary security interface to the class society.
* Own the annual penetration test of marine communication systems and robotics control infrastructure, tracking findings through to closure or formal risk acceptance.
* Conduct OT and vessel cyber security assessments across the fleet and robotic assets, coordinating with the HSEQ team on the safety-cyber interface, and travel up to 50% of the time depending on business need, typically averaging around 25%, both domestically and internationally, including offshore and to vessels and Remote Operations Centres, to do so.
* Support the cyber and information security of Remote Operations Centres, including shore-based centres and the aspirational mobile concept, and support secure remote-operation communications such as the move to TLS 1.3 or higher.
* Develop and maintain the programme documentation, standards and vessel and asset security tiering, monitor OT-specific threat intelligence, support defence-related assurance obligations including DISP, and brief leadership, clients and regulators on OT and vessel cyber security posture.
**Who you are**
* Experienced in operational technology or industrial control system cyber security, gained in a safety-critical environment such as maritime, offshore, energy, defence or heavy industry;
* Practised in applying IEC 62443 zones and conduits, or an equivalent OT security standard, to systems in service rather than on paper;
* Confident leading incident response in an operational environment, from identification through containment and recovery to post-incident review;
* Experienced in acting as the technical security point of contact for a class society, regulator or external auditor;
* Able to embed security into engineering work early, working alongside engineers as systems are designed, built and tested;
* Experienced in commissioning and managing penetration tests and tracking findings through to closure or formal risk acceptance;
* Able to produce security documentation, standards, assessments and control evidence to an auditable quality;
* Educated to degree level in a relevant technical discipline, or hold equivalent professional experience;
* Willing and able to travel up to 50% of the time, including offshore and to vessels;
* Eligible to work in the United States or the United Kingdom;
* Thoughtful, thorough and conscientious;
* Able to take ownership and engagement in the work;
* Able to work as a trusted advisor with senior stakeholders;
* Fun, Professional, Curious;
* Driven, proactive and able to work autonomously with little supervision, towards the company's purpose;
* A critical thinker and able to show initiative;
* Enthusiastic about protecting people and the planet.
**Desirable**
* Certified in a recognised OT or industrial cyber security qualification, such as IEC 62443 certification or GICSP;
* Experienced with autonomous or uncrewed systems, whether marine, aerial or ground;
* Familiar with DNV class notations and autonomous system assurance, including AROS;
* Familiar with defence security frameworks, including DISP;
* Experienced with satellite and marine communication systems and their security;
* Experienced in remote operations or control centre environments;
* Based within reach of a port environment or major airport hub.
**Salary for this position:**
United Kingdom: up to £115,000 base.
United States: up to $190,000 base. The maximum salary is offered to candidates who fully meet all the specified criteria. Where a candidate lacks certain skills or experience, the salary offered will be adjusted accordingly.
**Salary**: The salary varies for this position as we are recruiting in multiple regional locations and job grades. The salary process is based on skills, abilities, and experience required. **What you can expect:**
At Ocean Infinity, we believe in creating equal opportunities for all, celebrating each and everyone’s differences. We are driven by transforming the industry, through our technology, thoughts, behaviours and actions. Being inclusive and respectful to all is fundamental to who we are. It is the right thing to do and enables innovation and creativity to thrive.
There is more work to be done, and we know that we aren’t perfect, but our commitment to these values is unwavering. They are central to our mission and the impact we have on the industry, meaning, we cannot live without them.

## Risk & Compliance Lawyer
---
##### Office of General Counsel, London
Position details
Main information
---
* **Term type:**
Permanent
* **Working hours:**
9.30 am - 5.30 pm, Monday - Friday
* **Department:**
Office of General Counsel
* **Location:**
London
The firm
---
Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP is one of the world’s leading international law firms. The Firm was established in 1884 and has more than 2,000 lawyers. Headquartered in New York with offices in Beijing, Boston, Brussels, Hong Kong, Houston, London, Los Angeles, Luxembourg, Palo Alto, San Francisco, São Paulo, Singapore, Tokyo and Washington, D.C., the Firm provides coordinated legal advice and transactional capability to clients around the globe.
Description/Job Summary
---
We are seeking a Risk & Compliance Lawyer to join our London Risk & Compliance team, which sits within the OGC. 1-4 years legal experience is required in this fast paced environment. You will act as a key advisor for the team and firm.
Responsibilities/Duties
---
* Keeping abreast of changes and developments in relevant UK legal, regulatory and compliance obligations, including the SRA Standards and Regulations and firm authorization requirements;
* Advising on policy changes that will need to take place in line with regulatory developments and changes in law as required and draft amendments to such policies and associated guidance;
* Supporting partners and regulated individuals with queries regarding professional responsibility, ethics, confidentiality and disclosure obligations;
* Support the development and delivery of Risk & Compliance related training for the Firm and team;
* Working closely with the Firm's Director of Risk & Compliance (London) on broader risk and compliance projects;
* Supervising junior members of the Risk & Compliance team and offering guidance as appropriate;
* Working with key stakeholders and acting as a representative for the Firm's compliance function;
* Supporting the Firm with general risk and compliance queries;
* Supporting a culture of ethical awareness, accountability and risk management; and
* Other ad hoc duties as required.
Required Skills
---
* Previous experience within a compliance team is desirable;
* Fee earners with regulatory experience who are considering their first role within a Risk & Compliance team will also be welcomed;
* A high level of attention to detail;
* Excellent analytical skills;
* Ability to draft clearly and concisely;
* Excellent communication skills, written and verbal;
* The ability to influence and persuade at all levels
* Strong decision making capabilities;
* Team player;
* Must have sound judgment;
* Able to work in a fast paced environment;
* Good planning, time management and prioritisation skills; and
* Must have good knowledge of Microsoft office applications.
Required Education
---
* Bachelor's degree required (2:1 or above preferred);
* Must be qualified lawyer with 1-4 PQE;
Details
---
Salary and Benefits: Competitive
Hybrid: Monday-Thursday in office, ability to WFH on Fridays
Equal Opportunities
---
Simpson Thacher is committed to ensuring that everyone can reach their full potential, irrespective of background, identity, or circumstance. We know that we are at our best when we bring together diverse experiences and perspectives. This is why we are focused on fostering a collegial environment which maximises collaboration, empowering every individual to thrive and succeed.

## AML Analyst
---
##### Office of General Counsel, London
